# f2 = run. dot() takes two lists apart that the link knows to stay as made: nobody sees the steps, nothing runs between them, and what lies past the end reads as undefined either way: each step is a read under
# its written place, without a test of the place against the length and without a join. dot() is copied into the loop as a leaf that reads elements of a holder from in front is, the loop is built twice for the
# two lists, which are asked for their kind in front of the typed copy, and the six reads go by that kind in line. A short list and a hole give NaN; whole numbers are read out of their own kind.
# RUN: walk f2 mechanisms=all
